{
  "//": [
    "Q08 — Products never bought in a state (anti-join)",
    "What it answers: \"Which products has nobody in Texas ever bought?\"",
    "Route:           GET /products/dead   (params: state; every route also takes db=)",
    "Pattern:         anti_joins",
    "Engine:          MongoDB",
    "Think about it:",
    "In SQLite, knowing a purchase's state took joins to customers and zipcodes.",
    "Here state_code is copied into each purchase. Yet even idx_* scans all",
    "1,000,000 documents. Which index is missing? Create it in a copy and measure",
    "again. (The anti_joins pattern page shows another way to write this.)"
  ],
  "aggregate": "purchases",
  "cursor": {},
  "pipeline": [
    {
      "$match": {
        "state_code": "{{state}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "$group": {
        "_id": null,
        "bought": {
          "$addToSet": "$product_id"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "$lookup": {
        "from": "products",
        "let": {
          "bought": "$bought"
        },
        "as": "dead",
        "pipeline": [
          {
            "$match": {
              "$expr": {
                "$not": {
                  "$in": [
                    "$_id",
                    "$$bought"
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "$sort": {
              "_id": 1
            }
          },
          {
            "$limit": 100
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "$unwind": "$dead"
    },
    {
      "$replaceWith": "$dead"
    },
    {
      "$project": {
        "_id": 0,
        "product_id": "$_id",
        "product_name": 1
      }
    }
  ]
}
